VALUES ('m1', 'manish', 'Manish', 'Full-Stack Developer · Team Lead', 'React + Spring Boot systems that stay readable at 2am', '#4361EE',
  'I build responsive web applications and the scalable backend systems behind them, then make sure both ship on the same day.', 'Manish coordinates the crew: he turns a rough idea into a build plan, splits it into work that can land in a week, and reviews the parts he is not writing himself. He moved from Java services to React frontends and never gave up either, which is why most of the team''s architecture notes start with a database diagram.', 'I start most problems at the data layer. Once the entities and their transitions are honest, the API falls out of them and the interface stops being a negotiation. As team lead I care about two things: that a junior can open any repo here and find their way, and that what we demo on Friday was running in production on Thursday.', 'Write the failing case first, make it pass with the boring solution, then measure before optimising anything.',
  'Pair on the first draft of anything new, review everything else asynchronously with links instead of opinions.', '/images/avatars/manish.svg', 'Bengaluru, India', 'manish@fullstackcrew.example', NULL,
  NULL, NULL,
  '["React","TypeScript","Tailwind CSS","Java","Spring Boot","REST APIs","MySQL","JUnit","Git","GitHub Actions","Postman"]', '{"frontend":["React","TypeScript","Tailwind CSS","HTML","CSS"],"backend":["Java","Spring Boot","Spring Security","REST APIs"],"database":["MySQL","MongoDB"],"tools":["Git","GitHub","GitHub Actions","Postman","Docker"]}', '["pulseboard","a11y-radar","verdant-cart"]', '["Led the crew through three end-to-end product builds, from brief to deployed URLs.","Built the team''s shared CI workflow that runs type checks, tests and a Lighthouse pass on every pull request.","Introduced the accessibility checklist the team now clears before any UI review."]',
  '["API design","Performance budgets","Distributed transactions","Mentoring"]', '["Turning a vague request into a scoped, testable build plan","Debugging across the boundary between client and server","Keeping pull requests small enough to actually read"]', 0)
